las - an lwasm-compatible fork of the Microware RMA assembler, for building
NitrOS9 Level 2 software natively on the Foenix F256. Forked 2026-10-02 from
https://gitlab.com/debmint/rma at commit e82adeb (no upstream history kept).
Design and roadmap: ../docs/DESIGN.md

Original readme follows.

This is the Microware "rma" assembler which was provided by Microware for
the Tandy Color Computer.  This rendition should build on the Color Computer
as well as on Linux systems, Windows (under Mingw), and hopefully OSK.

This system, in conjunction with the C compiler and the RLink packages should
build programs and libraries that will work on the color computer or the
color computer emulators.

This package is released to the public domain in the hope that it will be
useful.

